        {
          "type": "legacy-html",
          "html": "GỐM MAKER IS A MELBOURNE BASED CERAMICS PRACTICE POSITIONED AT THE INTERSECTION OF CONTEMPORARY CRAFT AND CONCEPTUAL ART. THE BRAND IS GROUNDED IN PROCESS, NARRATIVE, AND CULTURAL REFERENCE, DRAWING FROM VIETNAMESE LANGUAGE AND MAKING TRADITIONS TO FRAME A QUIET, NON COMMERCIAL IDENTITY.THE VISUAL IDENTITY IS DELIBERATELY RESTRAINED, UTILISING MINIMAL TYPOGRAPHY, SOFT NEUTRAL TONES, AND GENEROUS NEGATIVE SPACE TO FOREGROUND THE WORK. PHOTOGRAPHY ACTS AS THE PRIMARY COMMUNICATION DEVICE, PRESENTING EACH PIECE WITH A GALLERY LIKE SENSIBILITY. DIGITALLY, THE WEBSITE FUNCTIONS AS AN EXTENSION OF THE PRACTICE RATHER THAN A TRANSACTIONAL PLATFORM. A SLOW, EDITORIAL LAYOUT AND SIMPLIFIED NAVIGATION PRIORITISE VIEWING AND REFLECTION OVER INTERACTION, REINFORCING THE BRAND’S CONTEMPLATIVE TONE."
        }
      ]
